{"id":"dry_ice","compound_name":"Graphs::Aero::dry_ice","source_path":"dry_ice/dry_ice.json","category":"Smoke","author":"Autodesk","description":"An aero simulation graph producing a dry ice effect","documentation_file":"dry_ice_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Dry Ice Graph\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph uses aero to create a dry ice simulation\n\n### Inputs and outputs \n\nInputs for this graph are the meshes acting as the source for the dry ice.  The output is the resulting aero dry ice volume.\n\n### Useful information\n\n- The key to obtaining the dry ice effect is using mesh noise on input geometry, along with `inherit velocity` and `initial velocity` to get the initial bubbling up, and negative `temperature` for the dry ice to then fall down.  The magnitude and speed of noise, and the scale of inherit/initial velocities will have to be adjusted depending on your geometry and scale.  Additionally, a significant network of influences is added to obtain the necessary detail and behavior for this effect.\n\n- Performance is directly related to the `fluid detail size` on the source air node.  The dry ice effect requires a high level of detail to look realistic, and so can be tricky to optimize.  One method used in this graph is leveraging auto-adaptivity to coarsen areas where the fog detail is lower.  \n\n- Scene scale affects the behavior of the simulation dramatically, set the `scene units in meters` accordingly, or scale your geometry.  Large geometry/scene units will produce slower moving smoke\n\n### Example scene\n\n- The example scenes puts this effect in context by providing a bowl for the dry ice to pour out from and slide against. Proper lighting and shading also plays an important role. Detail size is decreased to showcase the effect in full detail. Be advised that this will impact performance","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","fluids":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9","scatter":"2.15.0.9","simulation":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"cube_mesh","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"out_geometry","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"out_geometry1","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}],"counts":{"nodes":33,"connections":43,"values":126,"compounds":4},"node_types":{"Rendering::Materials::assign_material":4,"Simulation::Influence::modulate_influence":3,"Core::Math::multiply":3,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_cube":2,"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat":2,"Simulation::Aero::aero_solver_settings":1,"Simulation::Common::collider":1,"Simulation::Aero::source_air":1,"Simulation::Influence::vorticity_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::drag_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::turbulence_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::modifier_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::dissipation_influence":1,"Simulation::Aero::simulate_aero":1,"Simulation::Aero::aero_adaptivity_settings":1,"dummy_geo":1,"Rendering::Arnold::Arnold_standard_volume_mat":1,"mesh_noise":1,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere":1,"assign_gray_shader":1,"Core::Time::time":1,"Core::Randomization::curl_noise":1,"Modeling::Points::displace_points":1,"Geometry::Properties::get_point_position":1},"edge_type_pairs":{"Rendering::Materials::assign_material -> ":4,"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat -> Rendering::Materials::assign_material":3," -> Core::Math::multiply":3,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_cube -> Rendering::Materials::assign_material":2,"Core::Math::multiply -> Core::Randomization::curl_noise":2,"Simulation::Influence::modulate_influence -> Simulation::Influence::turbulence_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::drag_influence -> Simulation::Influence::modulate_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::modulate_influence -> Simulation